# Secrets — never commit (NFR-5)
# `.env` alone left copies unprotected — a .env.bak / .env~ / .env.local from an
# editor, a tool, or a hand-made backup is the same secrets in a tracked file.
# Ignore every .env* and re-admit only the committed template.
.env*
!.env.example
credentials/*.json

# Logs
logs/*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Generated outputs (contain team attendance/salary/performance data — never commit)
Attendance/
Salary_Slips/
# Everything in Result/ is generated. Listing extensions let the scorecard
# dashboard (.html, and it names individual developers' scores) slip through;
# ignore the directory and keep it on clone the way logs/ and credentials/ do.
Result/*
!Result/.gitkeep

# Intermediate image assets (the committed logo is assets/stacx_banner.jpg)
assets/*.png
